1.Create an HTML form for a Flipkart-style product review, including input fields for username, rating (as a dropdown from 1 to 5), 
and a textarea for the review message. Use appropriate labels for each field.
2.Add HTML5 validation attributes to your review form so that username is required, rating must be selected, and the review message must be at least 
20 characters long.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Use required, minlength, and a default unselectable option for the dropdown.</em>
3.Modify your form to use the POST method and, after submitting a test review, open the DevTools Network tab to preview the POST request data sent by your form.
<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Look for the form submission request and expand the payload/details to see your input values.</em>

Answer.
<html>
<head>
    <title>Flipkart Product Review</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin: 20px; }
        .form-group { margin-bottom: 15px; }
        label { display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; font-weight: bold; }
        input, select, textarea { width: 100%; max-width: 400px; padding: 8px; box-sizing: border-box; }
        button { padding: 10px 15px; background-color: #2874f0; color: white; border: none; cursor: pointer; }
        button:hover { background-color: #1259c7; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h2>Write a Flipkart Product Review</h2>

    <!-- Using POST method as required in Task 3 -->
    <form action="/submit-review" method="POST">
        
        <!-- Username Field -->
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="username">User Name:</label>
            <input type="text" id="username" name="username" required placeholder="Enter your full name">
        </div>

        <!-- Rating Dropdown -->
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="rating">Rating (1 to 5):</label>
            <select id="rating" name="rating" required>
                <!-- Default unselectable option -->
                <option value="" disabled selected>-- Select a Rating --</option>
                <option value="1">1 - Very Poor</option>
                <option value="2">2 - Poor</option>
                <option value="3">3 - Average</option>
                <option value="4">4 - Good</option>
                <option value="5">5 - Excellent</option>
            </select>
        </div>

        <!-- Review Message Textarea -->
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="review">Review Message:</label>
            <textarea id="review" name="review" rows="5" required minlength="20" placeholder="Write your review here (at least 20 characters)..."></textarea>
        </div>

        <!-- Submit Button -->
        <button type="submit">Submit Review</button>

    </form>

</body>
</html>


4.Build a Zomato-style food order form with inputs for user name, a select dropdown for food item (at least 3 options), quantity (number input), 
and a textarea for delivery instructions. Ensure all fields are labeled and use required validation.
5.Add a disabled input field to your food order form that displays a fixed order ID (e.g., ORD12345) and explain in a 
comment why this field should be disabled for users.

Answer.
<html>
<head>
    <title>Zomato Food Order</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin: 20px; }
        .form-group { margin-bottom: 15px; }
        label { display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; font-weight: bold; }
        input, select, textarea { width: 100%; max-width: 400px; padding: 8px; box-sizing: border-box; }
        input[disabled] { background-color: #e9ecef; cursor: not-allowed; }
        button { padding: 10px 15px; background-color: #cb202d; color: white; border: none; cursor: pointer; }
        button:hover { background-color: #a0131e; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h2>Zomato - Place Your Food Order</h2>

    <form action="/place-order" method="POST">
 
            EXPLANATION FOR DISABLED ORDER ID FIELD:
            The Order ID is generated automatically by the backend/system to uniquely identify an order.
            It is set to 'disabled' so that users cannot alter, tamper with, or accidentally change 
            the unique reference code assigned to their transaction.
  
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="order-id">Order ID:</label>
            <input type="text" id="order-id" name="order_id" value="ORD12345" disabled>
        </div>

        <!-- User Name Field -->
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="customer-name">Full Name:</label>
            <input type="text" id="customer-name" name="customer_name" required placeholder="Enter your full name">
        </div>

        <!-- Food Item Dropdown -->
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="food-item">Select Food Item:</label>
            <select id="food-item" name="food_item" required>
                <option value="" disabled selected>-- Choose an item --</option>
                <option value="butter_chicken">Butter Chicken with Naan</option>
                <option value="paneer_biryani">Hyderabadi Paneer Biryani</option>
                <option value="margherita_pizza">Classic Margherita Pizza</option>
                <option value="masala_dosa">Special Masala Dosa</option>
            </select>
        </div>

        <!-- Quantity Field -->
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="quantity">Quantity:</label>
            <input type="number" id="quantity" name="quantity" min="1" max="10" required placeholder="1">
        </div>

        <!-- Delivery Instructions Textarea -->
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="instructions">Delivery Instructions:</label>
            <textarea id="instructions" name="instructions" rows="4" required placeholder="e.g., Leave at the door, ring the bell, less spicy..."></textarea>
        </div>

        <!-- Submit Button -->
        <button type="submit">Place Order</button>

    </form>

</body>
</html>

